>
  <p>Before you can change a building, you have to know what is there. That sounds obvious, but it is the step that gets skipped most often, and skipping it is where a lot of project problems begin.</p>

  <p>As-built drawings are how you know what is there. They are the foundation of the project in the same way a concrete foundation is the base of a house. Everything else sits on top of them.</p>

