figcaption></figure>

  <p>Now the cabinet has to be rebuilt, the installer has to come back, and the countertop that was cut to match has to be redone. A small error on paper turned into weeks of delay and a real cost.</p>

  <p>The same thing happens with walls that are not where the plan shows them, ceilings that are lower than expected, and windows that were moved years ago.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">A mistake costs more the later you find it</div>
    <p>On paper, fixing a wrong measurement takes a few minutes. Once materials are ordered, it costs money. Once things are built, it costs a lot more. As-builts move the surprises to the very start, when they are cheapest to deal with.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>"But I already have the plans"</h2>

  <p>Many owners do have a set of old plans. They are useful, but they have two problems.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>The building was not built exactly like the plans.</strong> Small changes are made during construction and rarely drawn.</li>
    <li><strong>The building has changed since.</strong> Remodels, additions, new equipment, and repairs add up over the years.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>We cover this in more detail in <a href="/resources/as-built-drawings-vs-original-plans/">As-Built Drawings vs. Original Plans</a>.</p>

  <h2>The best time to get as-builts</h2>

  <p>At the very beginning, before design starts. That way your designer works from real numbers from the first day, and everyone after them does too.</p>

  <p>It is also a small part of the budget. A floor plan starts at $750, the site visit takes about 30 minutes for a typical home, and floor plans are delivered within 3 days. Compared to one reordered set of cabinets, it is inexpensive insurance.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Design, permits, pricing, and construction all depend on knowing what is there.</li>
    <li>As-built drawings are how you know.</li>
    <li>Getting them first is far cheaper than finding the problems during construction.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If you have a project coming up, you can <a href="/quote/">get an instant quote</a> in about a minute.</p>
